<title>USA: CCC seeks up to 7,000 T wheat for Kyrgyzstan.</title>
<headline>CCC seeks up to 7,000 T wheat for Kyrgyzstan.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Credit Corp said it seeks up to 7,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 or better wheat, excluding unclassed, mixed and durum wheat, under the export donation program to Kyrgyzstan.</p>
<p>Shipment period is set for October 15-November 10 and offers are due by September 26.</p>
<p>The wheat must be tested for vomitoxin and originate in areas of the U.S. where Karnal Bunt is not known to occur.</p>
<p>The CCC is part of the U.S. Department of Agriculture.</p>
<p>--Doris Frankel 312-983-7305</p>
